sequenceDiagram
    title Invariant — GOT[M].slot[k] is single-writer per slot, atomic-readable by many

    participant PWa as Priority Worker (codegen batch 1)
    participant PWb as Priority Worker (codegen batch 2)
    participant Slot as GOT[M].slot[foo]
    participant Caller1 as Runtime caller A
    participant Caller2 as Runtime caller B

    Note over Slot: invariant: slot has one writer at a time.<br/>readers atomic-load and dispatch

    Note over Slot: Phase 1 — initial codegen
    PWa ->> Slot: atomic store(ptr1)
    Note over Slot: ptr1 → batch-1 code

    Caller1 ->> Slot: atomic load
    Slot -->> Caller1: ptr1
    Caller1 ->> Caller1: call (in-flight)

    Note over Slot: Phase 2 — REPL redefines foo (new batch)
    PWb ->> Slot: atomic store(ptr2)
    Note over Slot: swap-before-drop ordering —<br/>new ptr written before any retention root drops<br/>(see concurrency-jit-retention)

    Caller2 ->> Slot: atomic load
    Slot -->> Caller2: ptr2
    Caller2 ->> Caller2: call (sees new code)

    Note over Caller1: Caller1's in-flight call returns.<br/>does NOT retain code address — language fn values<br/>are heap closures that go through GOT

    Note over Slot: Phase 3 — old retention root unreferenced<br/>(reclaim is the JIT-retention invariant —<br/>see concurrency-jit-retention)
